{"files": [{"id": 39621158, "name": "ppat.1011232.g002.tif", "size": 317236, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/39621158", "supplied_md5": "90c576dea64ad652478296e7b67f6dba", "computed_md5": "90c576dea64ad652478296e7b67f6dba", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 139140, "full_name": "Tian Xia", "first_name": "Tian", "last_name": "Xia", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 10164, "full_name": "Xin Wu", "first_name": "Xin", "last_name": "Wu", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Xin_Wu", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797226, "full_name": "Eunjin Hong", "first_name": "Eunjin", "last_name": "Hong", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797229, "full_name": "Kyle Jung", "first_name": "Kyle", "last_name": "Jung", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797232, "full_name": "Chih-Jen Lai", "first_name": "Chih-Jen", "last_name": "Lai", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797235, "full_name": "Mi-Jeong Kwak", "first_name": "Mi-Jeong", "last_name": "Kwak", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797238, "full_name": "Hogyu Seo", "first_name": "Hogyu", "last_name": "Seo", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 2560966, "full_name": "Stephanie Kim", "first_name": "Stephanie", "last_name": "Kim", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 583925, "full_name": "Zhongyi Jiang", "first_name": "Zhongyi", "last_name": "Jiang", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14797241, "full_name": "Inho Cha", "first_name": "Inho", "last_name": "Cha", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 9611629, "full_name": "Jae U. Jung", "first_name": "Jae U.", "last_name": "Jung", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Glucosylceramide_biosynthesis_pathway_is_essential_for_HRTV_infection_/22278536", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p><b>A.</b> Diagram of glycosphingolipid biosynthesis pathway. Genes highlighted in red were identified from CRISPR/Cas9 screen. <b>B-C.</b> Effect of NB-DNJ or UGT8-IN on HRTV replication. 293T cells were pre-treated with NB-DNJ or UGT8-IN for 24 hours before infection with HRTV (MOI = 1). Viral RNAs of the S-segment and M-segment were measured by qPCR and normalized to <i>GAPDH</i> mRNA. Data shown are means \u00b1 SEM from representative experiments (n = 3 technical replicates). <i>P</i> values were determined by ordinary one-way ANOVA with Dunnett\u2019s multiple comparison tests. ****, <i>P</i>\u2009<\u20090.0001; ***, <i>P</i> < 0.001; **, <i>P</i> < 0.01; *, <i>P</i> < 0.05. <b>D-E.</b> Effect of NB-DNJ and UGT8-IN on HRTV or rVSV-DBV infection. To generate a replication-competent rVSV-DBV, the VSV glycoprotein in its genome was replaced with DBV Gn/Gc. After incubation with indicated drugs for 24 hours, half-log serially diluted HRTV or rVSV-DBV was added to 4 replicate wells of a 96-well plate containing 293T cells for 72 hours. TCID<sub>50</sub> was calculated by plotting cell viability versus dilution factor using GraphPad Prism and fitted by a dose-response (variable slope) algorithm. <b>F.</b> Heat map of the levels of intracellular GalCer and GlcCer in 293T cells with or without NB-DNJ treatment.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 317236, "created_date": "2023-03-15T17:35:12Z", "modified_date": "2023-07-14T17:12:05Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["recombinant viruses pseudotyped", "potential therapeutic target", "group binding pocket", "glucose ceramide glucosyltransferase", "dabie bandavirus glyc